==Enemy==
Zuche is a glass cannon who runs at the speed of a [[Doge Dark]], burrows once, revives with 100% HP and has rapid and ''highly'' damaging multi-hit attacks, but has short range and low health; two or three [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]] hits are enough to put him out of commission, and many [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic]]/[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] units can take him out in one shot. However, he has strong pushing power and can deal heavy damage to your backliners if he burrows into them.

In short, he can be recognized as the opposite of his [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] counterpart, [[Duche]], as Duche is a tank with high health but low attack power.

==Strategy==
Being a rusher-type enemy that will often hit backliners after burrowing, Zuche can be quite a threat as a support enemy. There are two main approaches to dealing with him, both relying on his pseudo-Long Distance properties:

The first is by having an attacker cover where he resurfaces that can kill him quickly, such as [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] or [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]].

The second option is to treat him even closer to a [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemy]] by having few main attackers that will be where he resurfaces. If you take this approach, [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]] is extremely important for stalling him. This approach is great in [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]-focused stages, where long-ranged attackers are often not necessary.

If there are no other threatening Zombies in the stage, a well-timed [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] can neutralize Zuche by unburrowing him near instantly and freezing him for a few seconds.

